WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:03.690
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.630
Playmaker infiltrated the data bank?

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:08.920
Drive him out!

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.660
Umm, but that's not possible.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.800
Other intruders inside the data bank!

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.800
What?

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.670
Zaizen!

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.900
Zaizen...

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.560
I was waiting for you, Playmaker.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.730
I run Across the universe

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.900
At the speed of light

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.770
Begin Loading

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:57.500
Open the door of dreams

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.070
VRAINS spreads

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.180
Believe in myself

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.710
VRAINS continues

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:13.020
The circuit draws the future

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.090
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.690
Access!

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.390
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.000
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.300
Link with my soul

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.070
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.800
Now Win the Race

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.640
Connected world

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:36.140
No matter when

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.510
Nothing is impossible

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.650
Strive for hope

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.220
And ride the wind!

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.570
Zaizen!

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.520
Yusaku...

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.800
Brother?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.460
Why are you here?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.410
This is SOL Technologies' core.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:47.240
Data is processed and released from here.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.540
Playmaker.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.990
Zaizen and Ghost Girl, why are you here?

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.360
Were you waiting for me?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.200
That's not quite right.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.330
We're also interested in the data here.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.300
And this is a hard place to break into.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.300
I see.  I understand now.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.310
They used us as a decoy.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:20.310
She gave us the backdoor route 
so that they could get inside?

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.150
So she lost our duel on purpose?

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.120
Unfortunately, that's incorrect.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.720
But if I won that duel, 
I would've acquired you.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.940
But since I lost, I set up this break-in.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.590
So either result is fine.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.800
How cunning!

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.310
It's an honor to be praised by an AI.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.080
She's so positive!

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.440
Move out of the way, Zaizen.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.910
I can't let you go any further.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.510
So you know what's stored here?

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.510
I just learned about it.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:59.050
What happened ten years 
ago at SOL Technologies.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:02.100
And what happened to you.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:06.790
No way!  SOL Technologies was 
involved in the incident?

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.660
What does he mean?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.630
I have the right to learn what's stored here.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.470
You must be a victim from 
the incident ten years ago.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.170
What incident?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:27.180
I don't know what he's talking about, but 
I feel everyone here shouldn't find out.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.140
Send this footage to my office!

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.140
I'll record it in my office!

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.880
Turn off all the monitors!

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.630
And don't record it!  If 
you disobey, you're fired!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.630
How many times are we going to be fired?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.090
Who knows.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.180
If you know what happened, 
hand over the data.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.890
I can't.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.410
They looked at the data, 
but they won't show us?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.100
He's so petty.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.620
You're the Ignis.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:10.840
That's right!

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.070
I'm the great Ignis that 
you're searching for!

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.940
I lost my memories, so 
they named me like a dog.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:21.480
But that data contains my name, right?

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.810
It didn't.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.260
What's with this AI?

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.420
Does this AI have free 
will, like Revolver said?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:36.460
Playmaker, please give 
me that AI and back off.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:41.190
I promise to bring this incident 
to light and uncover the truth.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:46.790
As a FYI, Akira was demoted due 
to that situation with Revolver.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.880
Wow!  You gave up a successful 
career for your sister?

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.400
What a wonderful brother!

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.290
But he came this far to learn the truth.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.500
He's not messing around.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:03.500
No matter the reason, I won't 
let others handle this.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:08.410
#1: I'll personally uncover 
the truth about the incident.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:11.540
#2: This has nothing to do with you.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:17.360
#3: But if you insist on getting 
involved, you know how to stop me.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.820
A duel?

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.090
That's right.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:23.410
If you win, I'll accept your demands.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:27.450
I'll trust you, give you this AI, and leave.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.320
What?

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.970
But if I win, you leave.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:37.040
A duel is the only way to stop you.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:41.480
Fine!  I challenge you to a duel!

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:42.860
I accept!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.220
This always happens.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.920
I knew this would happen.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.890
Akira's deck is very tough.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:59.000
Yusaku, you must acquire the data!

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:00.320
Let's begin!

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:01.550
Duel!

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.450
I'll go first.  My turn!

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.660
I set a monster.

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:15.610
I Special Summon Tindangle Base 
Gardna in defense position!

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:19.350
What?  He already Special Summoned!

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:23.920
When a monster is set on your 
field, you can Special Summon

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.720
this card from your hand in defense position.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.820
I set a card and end my turn.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:32.830
Two monsters in defense position.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.830
His dueling is stiff, just like him.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:40.480
2300 DEF is a strong defense, 
but it can't stop me.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.110
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:51.220
I discard Stack Reviver to Special 
Summon Bitlooper from my hand!

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:56.390
By discarding a Level 2 or lower monster, 
I can Special Summon Bitlooper.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.980
Next, I summon Cyberse Gadget!

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.470
When it's summoned, I can negate the effects

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:06.630
of a Level 2 or lower 
monster in my graveyard...

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.700
...and Special Summon it in defense position.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.800
Resurrect, Stack Reviver!

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:14.040
Here it comes!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.240
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:24.010
I set Bitlooper, Cyberse 
Gadget and Stack Reviver!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.520
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.000
Link Summon!

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:36.400
Appear, Link 3!

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:42.700
Decode Talker!

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:50.610
Now that's a back you can count on!

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.850
Cyberse Gadget's effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:08:54.850 --> 00:09:02.690
When it's sent from the field to the 
graveyard, I Special Summon one Gadget Token!

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.050
And when I use Stack 
Reviver to Link Summon...

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:11.630
...I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower Cyberse in defense position.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.600
I resurrect Cyberse Gadget!

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:20.520
Decode Talker's effect!

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.540
Power Integration!

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:28.010
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for 
every monster it's linked to!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:38.220
Decode Talker's ATK is much higher 
than Tindangle Base Gardna's DEF!

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.490
Are you sure?

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.060
Tindangle Base Gardna's effect!

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:48.970
When a monster is Special Summoned next 
to the opponent's Link Monster's link...

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:54.720
...you can tribute this card to Special 
Summon a Tindangle from your hand.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:56.670
It ran away!

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:58.410
I don't run.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:01.430
I Special Summon Tindangle Hound!

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.220
What a scary pooch!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.570
But Decode Talker still has higher ATK!

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:21.250
Don't get impatient.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:23.030
Tindangle Hound's effect!

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.960
Hell Howling!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:33.580
The opponent's linked monsters lose 1000 ATK 
for every monster that they're linked to.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:37.850
I feel woozy...  I've gotten duelsick...

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.190
Be quiet.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:43.050
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Lemoine Point!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:47.600
When there are no monsters on the 
field, this card is destroyed.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:50.400
When there's a Tindangle on the field...

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.770
...you can't attack facedown 
monsters in defense position!

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:56.370
We can't attack!

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:59.120
Now what will you do?

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:03.740
Now what will you do?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.370
In that case...  Appear!

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.430
The circuit that leads to the future!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.690
Another Link Summon?

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:20.740
I set Cyberse Gadget and Gadget Token!

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.800
Link Summon!

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:30.120
Appear, Link 2 Flame Administrator!

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:33.960
1200 ATK?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.610
What can you do with that monster?

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:38.320
We can do this!

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:44.920
When Flame Administrator is on the field, 
Link Monsters on my field gain 800 ATK!

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:48.940
Decode Talker is linked to fewer 
monsters, so it gains ATK.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:53.640
Due to Tindangle Hound's effect, 
Flame Administrator loses ATK.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:57.530
And due to Flame Administrator's 
effect, ATK increases!

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.440
Ta daa!

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.130
Now Decode Talker has more ATK than yours!

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:08.380
Battle!  Decode Talker, 
attack Tindangle Hound!

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.540
Decode End!

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:22.020
You did it, Playmaker!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:24.120
Brother...

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:30.360
Tindangle Hound's effect ends, so 
our monsters regain their power!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.230
But Tindangle Hound's effect activates!

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:41.970
When it's sent to the graveyard, your 
facedown monster switches to faceup defense position.

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:45.940
I switch my facedown monster to faceup!

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.910
Appear, Tindangle Angel!

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:56.250
Tindangle Angel's effect activates!

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:59.680
A Flip Effect Monster in 
your hand or graveyard...

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:03.340
...is Special Summoned in 
facedown defense position.

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:09.070
I Special Summon Tindangle Hound from my 
graveyard in facedown defense position!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.310
The pooch is back!

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:17.540
When this effect activates during 
your Battle Phase, the battle ends!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:20.440
Whoa!  He ended the battle!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.510
I set a card and end my turn.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:28.480
I see.  His deck is a 
Flip Effect Monster Deck.

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:31.800
It's a unique and interesting deck.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.060
This isn't the time to act confident.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:37.630
The opponent clearly has the advantage.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.000
That's true.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:45.020
That scary pooch has a dangerous 
effect, but its Flip Effect is worse.

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:51.310
Playmaker, are you about the same age as Aoi?

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.280
You probably are.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:59.940
In that tragedy ten years ago, I 
don't know the pain you endured.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:04.520
But I do know the pain of losing someone.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.530
What's he talking about?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.840
Ten years ago, Aoi and I 
suddenly lost our parents.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.010
He's about to tell a story.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.500
Be quiet.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.540
Okay.

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:25.220
It was our parents' second 
marriage, each with a child.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:28.310
They went on vacation for 
their wedding anniversary...

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:31.150
...and got into a traffic accident.

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:35.570
I was sixteen years old.  Aoi was six.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.480
It was too sudden.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.630
Aoi and I didn't even have time to mourn.

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:51.840
Many strangers arrived, stealing 
our parents' inheritance.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:58.810
We didn't know the ways of the world, 
but we were thrown into its chaos.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:01.280
It was a painful time.

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:10.620
We did anything to live, even dirty work.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.860
You're a hacker who'll do anything for money?

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.330
But you're still a kid.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.580
Don't underestimate me because I'm a kid!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.430
I like your spirit.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:24.660
Let's see if it'll last for five minutes.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:26.140
Sit over there.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:28.870
Break it in five minutes.

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.980
If you fail, I'll break your arms.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:36.660
I was focused on staying alive.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.850
In order to live, I had to fight on my own.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.360
Well done.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.100
Here's your reward.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:16:01.380
Each day wore down my spirit, 
but Aoi kept me going.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.480
Let's go get some hot food.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:16.650
I must protect Aoi.

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:20.690
I won't let this six year-old be unhappy.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.180
That's all I thought about.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:28.170
If Aoi experienced what you did...

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:31.360
If a stranger kidnapped her...

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:36.560
My spirit would've broken.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.840
Kidnap?

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:41.600
SOL Technologies?

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.680
What's he saying?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.390
How dare you...

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.880
I ask one last time!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.960
Trust me and let me handle everything!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.830
You know nothing...

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:02.380
About me...

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:05.340
You know nothing about me!

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:10.640
Zaizen, you're probably a good person.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.650
But you don't know me!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:17.750
You only know a fictional version of me!

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:22.490
Playmaker, you're going to keep fighting?

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:25.180
He's still talking?

00:17:25.180 --> 00:17:28.820
Let's hurry up and defeat him, Playmaker!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:33.040
But I won't lose so easily.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.470
Then let's see what you can do.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.840
Fine!  So be it!

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.310
He's into it now!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.510
My turn.  I draw!

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.980
I Flip Summon Tindangle Hound!

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.900
Tindangle Hound's Flip Effect activates!

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:07.260
It targets another monster on the field.

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:14.710
This card gains ATK equal to the target, and 
the target switches to facedown defense position.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:18.240
I select Tindangle Angel!

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:22.680
Tindangle Hound gains its ATK!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:27.650
Tindangle Angel switches to 
facedown defense position!

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:30.750
I knew it had an annoying effect!

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:34.730
Tindangle Hound's effect again!

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.690
Hell Howling!

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:41.630
Battle!

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.940
Tindangle Hound attacks Flame Administrator!

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:58.120
Since Flame Administrator is gone, your 
Link Monster's ATK drops back to normal.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:07.120
And since Decode Talker lost a monster 
that was linked to it, it loses more ATK!

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:16.200
Decode Talker's back used to look 
so big, but it now looks small.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:21.580
But Decode Talker gains 1000 ATK.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:24.540
I expected that.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:25.410
Oh.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:27.380
I set one card.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.080
I end my turn.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:32.350
Hell's guard dog protects an angel...

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:36.220
Those monsters are like Akira and Aoi.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.250
The brother protects the sister.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:42.380
If the brother loses, the 
sister resurrects the brother.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.810
A siblings' bond is unbreakable.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.830
This is a tough combo.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.560
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.770
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.940
I summon Balancer Lord!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:03.710
I activate my Continuous Trap, Limit Code!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:11.460
I put a Limit Counter on this card for 
every Cyberse Link Monster in my graveyard!

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:16.930
There's one Cyberse Link Monster in 
my graveyard, Flame Administrator.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:27.050
I Special Summon a Code Talker from my 
Extra Deck and equip it with this card!

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:31.300
I Special Summon Encode 
Talker from my Extra Deck!

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:36.980
Decode Talker's effect!

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:38.870
Power Integration!

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:45.820
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for 
every monster that's linked to it!

00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:47.320
That's pointless!

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.890
Tindangle Hound's effect!

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.370
Hell Howling!

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:56.500
Not again.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:21:02.810
The fact that his power down is stronger 
than Cyberse's power up hurts my pride.

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:07.680
My deck unleashes great 
power against Link Monsters.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:11.700
But it seems you don't know my true goal.

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:15.800
I bet my future on this!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:19.160
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:24.130
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters!

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:30.770
I set Balancer Lord and Link 3 
Encode Talker in the Link Markers!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:36.970
Link 4?

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.350
Link Summon!

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.220
Appear, Link 4!

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:48.540
Firewall Dragon!

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:54.560
A Link 4 Cyberse has appeared!

00:21:55.240 --> 00:22:02.400
It's Playmaker's ace monster 
that defeated Revolver!

00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:27.170
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.410 --> 00:22:30.690
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:31.110 --> 00:22:34.310
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.610 --> 00:22:38.360
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:42.250
Try It over and over

00:22:43.990 --> 00:22:50.410
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.760 --> 00:22:57.350
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.640 --> 00:22:59.910
Nothing is certain

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:01.590
In these isolated times

00:23:01.870 --> 00:23:03.340
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:05.110
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:08.510
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:12.080
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:16.050
The miracles we create

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:18.290
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:22.130
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:39.140
He could've chosen a peaceful life.

00:23:39.140 --> 00:23:42.520
Days of youth, talking about 
the future with friends.

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:48.910
But his innermost emotions 
couldn't accept this happy life.

00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:50.960
He wants to learn the truth.

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:55.130
So he didn't accept fate and fought back.

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:59.050
The incident from ten years 
ago hasn't ended at all!

00:23:59.050 --> 00:24:02.890
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Incident Buried in Darkness

00:24:02.890 --> 00:24:04.790
Into the VRAINS!
